 says = "None of the four recorded options answers the question, and the bound they argue over is not canon. `Width` is a count of bits over `u32`, and three of the ten associated constants carry values it cannot hold at all, so the first option is arithmetically impossible rather than merely costly. The bound the question inherits, that the door is two types and no more, is a sentence in the crate's design and appears nowhere in the canon. What the door carries out is the coordinate set of the ratified parameterisation, spelled in types the stack owns. **How many types that is, this ruling does not say**, because the two derivations disagree about the count and neither the canon nor a third reading settles it."
 promotion = "Two instances, blind and separately dispatched on different personas, each with its own committed probes and controls. Blindness is checkable rather than asserted: both worktrees were cut from `0cac9beb`, and the second seat's merge `2ff7ae29` is not an ancestor of the first seat's head `176ced90`, so neither branch could show the other's file to a `git log`.\n\n**What each varied, and the tier is over the intersection.** Seat 238 compiled the four options against a checked crate and against the exempt one: the first refused at three of the six constants with two controls building, the fourth measured at ten hard errors with four controls at zero, the third found to have no mechanism short of changing another repository, and the second's two stated costs both measured false. It also built the existence proof, a ten-coordinate door with an outside crate declaring a format at radix 3 with a negative exponent and a half-step phase, naming no machine type on any line. Seat 239 compiled the same first option and refuted it at `BASE` and `MIN` specifically, in shipped and tested code, and reached the same fifth answer from the constants rather than from the door.\n\n**They intersect on three things and each was measured on both instruments**: that no recorded option is correct, that the two-type bound does not survive, and that the coordinate set is what the door carries. Both also independently found the same defect in the question's own note, that `min_adt_const_params` is the wrong gate name, since it refuses the crate's real `Width` shape for having a private field on a public struct while `adt_const_params`, which the workspace register carries in its allowed tier, accepts the identical source.\n\n**They disagree about the count, and this ruling does not resolve it.** Seat 238 answers one type per coordinate; seat 239 answers however many the ten coordinates need, which it puts at more than two and fewer than ten, reserving whether the signed coordinates share a type. Two instances agree about the intersection of their claims and never the union, so the count is outside what this ratifies. An earlier draft of this row asserted seat 238's count in its `says` while also calling the division open, which is both an overreach and a contradiction inside one sentence.\n\n**The refusal count is three and an earlier draft said six.** What was measured is that three constants carry values `Width` cannot hold; the six is a claim about the declared types rather than the values, and two of those six ship only values `Width::bits` accepts, `Quantum::SLOPE` at 0 and 1 and `Format::PHASE_DEN` at 1 and 2. The arithmetic-impossibility conclusion rests on the three and does not need the six."
 because = "Under the settled ratification model the experts propose and the coordinator judges whether the reasoning, the evidence and the stated region are enough. The deciding fact is that the option list was refused by compilation rather than by argument, on two instruments that did not read each other, and that the refutation of the first option is arithmetic: a `u32` count cannot hold a negative bound, so no amount of design preference reopens it.\n\nThe question's own note argued for the first option on the ground that nine of the ten constants close under it. Seat 238 compiled the option and measured the figure at one; seat 239 refuted it separately at `BASE` and `MIN`, which are negative in shipped and tested code. Neither figure was in the registry, and the claim had stood there one build from refutation."
-note = "**The positive shape is ratified only as far as both seats reached, and no further.** Seat 238 proposes that the bound stop being a count of types and become a position rule, that in the introducing crate a bare primitive appear only in the constructor and accessor of a primitive that crate itself defines, plus the const generic parameter position. That is one instance and is recorded as a proposal rather than carried here. Seat 239 leaves the division of the signed coordinates open in the same terms.\n\n**A design correction is owed and is not this ruling's to make.** `arvo-format/DESIGN.md.tmpl:235` states the two-type bound as the crate's own design, and it is now known to be wrong. The design tier changes before the code under it does.\n\n**One test-gate finding travels with this**, from seat 238 and verified: `the_format_inventory_admits_a_member_this_crate_does_not_know_about` is the only test asserting the ratified open-inventory clause, and it lives inside the crate-wide exemption, so it asserts that clause in the one crate where the rule it is about cannot refuse anything. It is narrow twice, because its `Ternary` also borrows the crate's own ambient, quantum and slot range and so writes two of the ten coordinates rather than all of them."
+note = "**The positive shape is ratified only as far as both seats reached, and no further.** Seat 238 proposes that the bound stop being a count of types and become a position rule, that in the introducing crate a bare primitive appear only in the constructor and accessor of a primitive that crate itself defines, plus the const generic parameter position. That is one instance and is recorded as a proposal rather than carried here. Seat 239 leaves the division of the signed coordinates open in the same terms.\n\n**A design correction was owed when this was ratified, and it has landed.** `arvo-format`'s design stated the two-type bound as the crate's own. Under its heading \"The two primitives, and why they are here\" it now says the two are not the bound on what the door carries and that a count of types is not the bound at all, and it names the position rule of seat 238 as open rather than adopted, which is as far as this ruling goes.\n\n**One test-gate finding travels with this**, from seat 238 and verified: `the_format_inventory_admits_a_member_this_crate_does_not_know_about` is the only test asserting the ratified open-inventory clause, and it lives inside the crate-wide exemption, so it asserts that clause in the one crate where the rule it is about cannot refuse anything. It is narrow twice, because its `Ternary` also borrows the crate's own ambient, quantum and slot range and so writes two of the ten coordinates rather than all of them."
